        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0207" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg111"/>

                <head>No. 74.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 2, 1873</date>. (Received Dec. 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed I have the honor to transmit yon a
                    translated copy of the treaty of August 26, 1873, recently ratified by the
                    governments of Guatemala, Salvador, and Nicaragua, and which, without doubt,
                    will also be ratified by the new government that is proposed to be organized in
                    Honduras.</p>
                <p>I beg to call your attention to the fifth article, and to remark that I believe
                    in the four states named there is a strong and growing disposition to adopt the
                    principle of confederation. Costa Rica stands aloof now, because her people, in
                    my opinion, are opposed to confederation with the other states.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d76-a1.xml" xpointer="d76-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
